[{"id": "6eb533b", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "f3c0445", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "shortcode", "settings": {"shortcode": "[rank_math_breadcrumb]"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1d5c075", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Grooming tools: what each one does and which you need", "header_size": "h1"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e681221", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You want to buy the few tools your dog's coat actually needs, not a drawer full of gadgets, and to know which ones need extra care.</p>", "typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "982ba87", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>By Grooming Dogs · Updated {{UPDATED}}</p>", "text_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e9a1fd3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>This page is about <strong>choosing</strong> tools. How to use each one is covered in its own guide, linked in each section. Not sure what coat your dog has? <a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\">Identify your dog's coat first</a>.</p>", "typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "fc51f23", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "image", "settings": {"image": {"id": 32, "url": "https://grooming-dogs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/pexels-photo-4432261.jpeg", "alt": "A dog's paws on a towel beside a rubber grooming brush and a bottle of shampoo.", "source": "library"}, "image_size": "large", "caption_source": "custom", "caption": "Photo: Mathew Coulton / Pexels", "caption_typography_typography": "custom", "caption_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"caption_typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "caption_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "60b3375", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}}, "elements": [{"id": "a588fe6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Most dogs need a short list of tools:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>A brush that suits their coat, plus a comb</strong> to check your work <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>;</li><li><strong>dog nail clippers or a grinder,</strong> with styptic powder <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup>;</li><li><strong>a dog shampoo and a towel</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>;</li><li><strong>a soft toothbrush and pet toothpaste</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "e25a4fb", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Add an undercoat rake for double coats <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>, and blunt-ended scissors or small clippers with guide combs only if you'll do trims at home <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. A dryer is optional <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Your vet or groomer can suggest the right tools for your dog's coat <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "949e8d1", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "a0cf339", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "How to choose grooming tools", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "how-to-choose-grooming-tools"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "2ccd1e2", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Start from your dog, not the shop shelf:</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "89b658f", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ul><li><strong>Coat type decides the brush.</strong> The right brushing tools depend on the coat <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. Find your dog's coat group in <a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\">identify your dog's coat first</a>, then use the starter kits at the bottom of this page.</li><li><strong>Buy for the jobs you'll actually do.</strong> If a groomer handles haircuts, you don't need clippers.</li><li><strong>Choose tools that fit comfortably in your hand</strong> so you can work gently and safely <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Buy tools made for dogs</strong> where it matters, especially nail clippers, toothpaste and shampoo <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Ask for advice.</strong> Your vet or groomer can recommend tools for your dog's coat type <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "a38a2fb", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "e923525", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Brushes and combs", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "brushes-and-combs"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9419e10", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Most dogs need one main brush and a comb. Which brush depends on the coat. How to use them: see <a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/\">how to brush your dog properly</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c03a0a5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Slicker brush", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "72aedbe", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> fine wire bristles for working out tangles and removing loose, dead hair <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> long, silky and curly coats <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>, dense coats that tangle <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>, and the densest areas of double coats <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> use it gently, especially near the skin. A slicker is for small tangles, not tight mats. Tight mats need a groomer (see <a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/#dealing-with-mats\">dealing with mats</a>).</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "b6a0e98", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Pin brush", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1cebdd6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> a brush with spaced pins, used on longer coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> many long-haired dogs <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> on its own it doesn't check down to the skin. Follow with a comb.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "faa4893", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Bristle brush", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "04630f0", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> removes loose, dead hair and smooths the coat <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> short and medium coats, and some long coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. It's often used after a slicker or rubber brush <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> it works on the surface, so it won't get through tangles in a long or double coat.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "d7862ed", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Rubber curry brush", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c723209", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> a rubber brush that loosens dead hair, dirt and dead skin, and polishes smooth coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. It also helps spread the coat's natural oils <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> short and smooth coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. It's also used on wiry coats <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> it isn't designed to get through long or tangled coats.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "78bb1e7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Undercoat rake", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "ec51db4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> reaches into a thick undercoat to remove loose undercoat hair <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> double coats, alongside your regular brush <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> it's for double coats. Smooth, single-layer coats don't have an undercoat for it to work on.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9efbdca", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Comb", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "a0439d5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What it does:</strong> a steel comb lets you check your brushing has reached the skin, finish the coat and remove debris <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. A wide-toothed steel comb helps work gently through tangles <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. <strong>Suits:</strong> most coats that are long enough to tangle, especially long, silky, curly and double coats <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. <strong>Limitation:</strong> avoid combs with bent teeth, which can snag or damage the coat <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "b0a0a6b", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "bf2b9e4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "De-shedding tools", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "de-shedding-tools"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "b1a3519", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What they do:</strong> de-shedding tools, like undercoat rakes, remove loose undercoat. They're used for double coats, gently, in addition to regular brushing <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1952776", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Are they safe?</strong> Used gently and as directed, they're part of normal home care for double coats <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Like any tool that works close to the skin, they can irritate it if pressed hard or used for too long on one spot.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Use light pressure.</strong></li><li><strong>Follow the manufacturer's instructions.</strong></li><li><strong>Stop if the skin looks red or your dog seems uncomfortable.</strong> If the skin stays irritated, see <a href=\"/dog-grooming-problems/\">problems after grooming</a>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9e41279", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Not for:</strong> short and smooth coats, which don't have an undercoat to remove. A rubber curry brush is the usual tool for those coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "b0e176d", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "a81fc89", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Bathing and drying equipment", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "bathing-and-drying-equipment"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "fbde6c7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What you need</strong> (how to bathe: see <a href=\"/bathing-your-dog/\">how to bathe your dog</a>):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Shampoo made for dogs.</strong> Human hair products aren't designed for pets <sup><a href=\"#s9\" aria-label=\"Source 9\">[9]</a></sup>, and dog care organizations recommend dog-specific products <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>A towel.</strong> A microfiber towel absorbs well <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>A non-slip mat</strong> for the tub or shower, so your dog feels steady.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9013efa", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Is a dryer worth it?</strong> A dryer is optional <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Many dogs dry well enough</strong> with towels and a warm room.</li><li><strong>If you use one,</strong> choose a dryer with a cool or low setting. Hot settings can burn a dog's skin <sup><a href=\"#s9\" aria-label=\"Source 9\">[9]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Dryers made for dogs</strong> are used for some coat types <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>High-powered professional dryers are a groomer's tool.</strong> They're not needed for home bathing.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "b37479e", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "65fc4f3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Nail tools", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "nail-tools"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "992b2e4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>How to trim: see <a href=\"/trimming-dog-nails/\">how to trim your dog's nails</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "f4cc0b8", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<div class=\"gd-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Tool</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th><th scope=\"col\">Often suits</th><th scope=\"col\">Caveat</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Scissor- or plier-style clippers</strong></th><td>Two blades cross to cut the nail <sup><a href=\"#s7\" aria-label=\"Source 7\">[7]</a></sup></td><td>Plier styles for larger, thicker nails; scissor styles for small dogs <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup></td><td>Use clippers made for dogs <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Guillotine-style clippers</strong></th><td>The nail goes through a hole and a single blade cuts it <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup></td><td>Some owners prefer them <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td><td>Some veterinary guidance advises against them because they can crush the nail <sup><a href=\"#s7\" aria-label=\"Source 7\">[7]</a></sup>. Other dog organizations list them as a normal option <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Grinder</strong></th><td>Wears the nail down gradually <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup></td><td>Thicker nails, or dogs that dislike the feel of clippers <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup></td><td>Noisy, which some dogs find frightening <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup>. Keep clippers too, for spots a grinder can't reach <sup><a href=\"#s7\" aria-label=\"Source 7\">[7]</a></sup>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Styptic powder</strong></th><td>Helps stop bleeding if you cut a nail too short <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td><td>Every nail kit <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "346477e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Both clippers and grinders are safe when used correctly. Choose the one you're most comfortable with and that your dog tolerates best <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "15f9d0e", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "612f178", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Clippers, blades and scissors", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "clippers-blades-and-scissors"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "013f6ec", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You only need these if you'll do trims at home. What's realistic, and how: see <a href=\"/dog-haircuts-and-trimming/\">trimming at home</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "647f251", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Scissors:</strong> choose <strong>blunt-ended (round-tip) scissors</strong> for home trims around the face, feet and sanitary area <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Pointed grooming shears are a professional's tool.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "bd1715f", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Clippers:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>For home tidy-ups,</strong> choose <strong>small clippers with guide combs</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Guide combs clip onto the blade to control how long the hair is left <sup><a href=\"#s8\" aria-label=\"Source 8\">[8]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Detachable blades</strong> let you swap in a cool blade if one gets hot <sup><a href=\"#s8\" aria-label=\"Source 8\">[8]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Comfort:</strong> choose clippers that feel comfortable in your hand <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "2fa29f6", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "aad6284", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ul><li><strong>Blades heat up:</strong> clipper blades can get hot during use. Check them often <sup><a href=\"#s8\" aria-label=\"Source 8\">[8]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Damaged equipment:</strong> never use a damaged or broken blade or comb, because it can injure the skin <sup><a href=\"#s8\" aria-label=\"Source 8\">[8]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Tight mats:</strong> don't buy clippers or scissors to deal with tight mats yourself. That's a job for a groomer (see <a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/#dealing-with-mats\">dealing with mats</a>).</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "7303f24", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "22a0535", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Ear and dental supplies", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "ear-and-dental-supplies"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4064dc7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>For ears</strong> (how to clean: see <a href=\"/cleaning-dog-ears/\">cleaning your dog's ears</a>):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>A dog ear-cleaning solution,</strong> ideally one your vet recommends <sup><a href=\"#s10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a><a href=\"#s11\" aria-label=\"Source 11\">[11]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Real cotton balls or gauze</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a><a href=\"#s11\" aria-label=\"Source 11\">[11]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>No cotton swabs or pointed tools.</strong> They can push debris deeper and injure the ear <sup><a href=\"#s10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a><a href=\"#s11\" aria-label=\"Source 11\">[11]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>No hydrogen peroxide.</strong> The American Kennel Club advises against using it in dogs' ears <sup><a href=\"#s10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "a39ee48", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>For teeth</strong> (how to brush: see <a href=\"/brushing-dog-teeth/\">brushing your dog's teeth</a>):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>A soft-bristled toothbrush.</strong> Many owners start with a finger before moving to a brush <sup><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>A toothpaste made for pets,</strong> without added fluoride, never human toothpaste <sup><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Not needed:</strong> dental scrapers or scaling tools. Hardened tartar is a job for your vet.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "77e77c3", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "4e53808", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Starter kits by coat type", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "starter-kits-by-coat-type"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "33100d6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Everything below builds on a <strong>basic kit for every dog</strong>:</p>\n<ul><li>nail clippers or a grinder, plus styptic powder <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup>;</li><li>dog shampoo and a towel <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>;</li><li>a soft toothbrush and pet toothpaste <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>;</li><li>a vet-recommended ear cleaner and cotton balls <sup><a href=\"#s10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a><a href=\"#s11\" aria-label=\"Source 11\">[11]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4f3084d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Then add the brushing tools for your dog's coat. These are typical starting points, not rules. Individual dogs vary, and your groomer may suggest something different.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1ce4d65", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<div class=\"gd-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Coat group</th><th scope=\"col\">Brushing tools to start with</th><th scope=\"col\">Optional extras</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Short and smooth</strong></th><td>Rubber curry brush <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>; bristle brush <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup></td><td>—</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Wiry</strong></th><td>Rubber-bristled brush <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>; comb</td><td>Ask a groomer how the coat is best kept</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Double</strong></th><td>Undercoat rake or de-shedding tool <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>; slicker brush for dense areas <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>; steel comb <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup></td><td>Wide-toothed comb for tangles <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Long and silky</strong></th><td>Slicker or rubber-bristled brush, plus a steel comb <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>; a pin brush suits many long coats <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup></td><td>Blunt-ended scissors or small clippers with guide combs for home tidy-ups <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Curly</strong></th><td>Slicker or rubber-bristled brush, plus a steel comb <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup></td><td>Blunt-ended scissors or small clippers with guide combs for home tidy-ups <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "14aacde", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Not sure which row is your dog? See <a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\">identify your dog's coat first</a>. Comparing the cost of home tools with professional grooming? See <a href=\"/dog-grooming-cost/\">what grooming costs</a>. </p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "ce35fb8", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If your dog is frightened of a tool, especially clippers or a grinder, see <a href=\"/grooming-an-anxious-dog/\">if your dog is scared of grooming tools</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "214e66e", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "434cd1a", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Common questions", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "common-questions"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "11fecf5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "accordion", "settings": {"tabs": [{"_id": "c276706", "tab_title": "Do I need a slicker brush and an undercoat rake?", "tab_content": "<p>Only if your dog has a double coat. For double coats, an undercoat rake or de-shedding tool works alongside regular brushing <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>, and a slicker helps in the densest areas <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Most other coats need a slicker or a rubber brush plus a comb, but not a rake <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, {"_id": "5a6b5a8", "tab_title": "Is a dog grooming dryer worth it?", "tab_content": "<p>A dryer is optional <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Towel-drying and a warm room are often enough. If you do use a dryer, choose one with a cool or low setting, because hot dryers can burn a dog's skin <sup><a href=\"#s9\" aria-label=\"Source 9\">[9]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Dryers made for dogs are used for some coat types <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. See <a href=\"/bathing-your-dog/\">how to bathe your dog</a> for drying technique.</p>"}, {"_id": "7968315", "tab_title": "What should a beginner buy first?", "tab_content": "<p>Start with:</p>\n<ul><li>a brush that suits your dog's coat;</li><li>a comb;</li><li>dog nail clippers or a grinder, with styptic powder;</li><li>dog shampoo and a towel;</li><li>a soft toothbrush with pet toothpaste <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a><a href=\"#s12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a></sup>.</li></ul>\n<p>Add other tools only when you have a job for them.</p>"}], "title_html_tag": "h3", "faq_schema": "yes", "selected_icon": {"value": "fas fa-plus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "selected_active_icon": {"value": "fas fa-minus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "title_color": "#17324D", "tab_active_color": "#17324D", "__globals__": {"border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder", "title_color": "globals/colors?id=primary", "tab_active_color": "globals/colors?id=primary"}}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "8ea0224", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs"}}, "elements": [{"id": "99fc3aa", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p class=\"gd-label\" id=\"next\"><strong>Where to go next</strong></p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "007aebb", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "flex_wrap": "wrap", "flex_direction_mobile": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}}, "elements": [{"id": "b404141", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "bdf30c8", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\">Dog coat types</a></strong></p><p>Find your dog's coat group before you buy.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "f8d1616", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "77ef0a3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/\">How to brush your dog properly</a></strong></p><p>Getting the most from your brush and comb.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "bd81281", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "c307032", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/trimming-dog-nails/\">How to trim your dog's nails</a></strong></p><p>Using clippers or a grinder safely.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "e52b354", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FFFFFF", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurf", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 48}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "d2890fe", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong><a href=\"/dog-haircuts-and-trimming/\">Trimming and haircuts at home</a></strong></p><p>What's realistic with scissors and clippers.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "67bb607", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>This is general information about